<HelpTab>
    <HelpSection Title="Acknowledge">
        <FluentText>
            Press <strong>Acknowledge</strong> to tell other managers you've seen an alert and are dealing with it. It stays
            in the Open list, marked <strong>Acknowledged</strong> with your name and the time, and drops out of the count in
            the menu.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Resolve">
        <FluentText>
            Press <strong>Resolve…</strong> when the problem is dealt with. You can add a note about what was done, which
            other managers see in History. If the same problem happens again later, a new alert is raised.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Cleared automatically">
        <FluentText>
            Most alerts clear themselves when the problem goes away, and move to History marked <strong>Cleared
            automatically</strong>:
        </FluentText>
        <ul>
            <li>a kiosk that was offline comes back online;</li>
            <li>a kiosk that needed attention reports itself healthy again;</li>
            <li>a failing automation rule next runs without errors;</li>
            <li>someone who missed their clock-in clocks in;</li>
            <li>overdue training is completed, or an expiring document is renewed.</li>
        </ul>
        <FluentText>This happens whether or not someone acknowledged the alert first.</FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Notifications">
        <FluentText>
            Kiosk alerts send the same notifications as before (<strong>Kiosk offline</strong> and <strong>Kiosk needs
            attention</strong>). A failing automation rule sends an <strong>Automation rule failed</strong> notification
            the first time it fails, not on every run. A missed clock-in sends <strong>Missed clock-in</strong> by push.
            Overdue training and expiring documents are checked every hour and arrive as one <strong>Training overdue</strong>
            or <strong>Staff documents expiring</strong> notification for everything new that hour, rather than one each.
            Each person can turn these on or off, by push or email, under Notifications on their account page.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpNote>Resolved alerts are kept for 90 days, then deleted.</HelpNote>
</HelpTab>
